12
00:49:38,181 --> 00:49:44,181
Hotel Transylvania is a 2012 American animated monster comedy film directed by Genndy Tartakovsky, written by Peter Baynham and Robert Smigel, and featuring
the voices of Adam Sandler, Andy Samberg, Selena Gomez, Kevin James, Fran Drescher, Steve Buscemi, Molly Shannon, David Spade, and CeeLo Green.

13
00:53:46,363 --> 00:53:52,363
It tells the story of Count Dracula, who is the owner of Hotel Transylvania,
where the world's monsters can take a rest from human civilization.

14
00:57:54,545 --> 00:58:00,545
When the "human-free hotel" is unexpectedly visited by a human traveler named Jonathan, Drac must do everything in his power to prevent his daughter
Mavis and the other guests from finding out that a human has found their safe place, which may jeopardize the hotel's future and his career.

15
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
As a first-time feature director, Tartakovsky set out to make a film that used his background in traditional animation to implement the physics of 2D in
computer animation, inspired by the physical comedy of Tex Avery, and departing from the focus on realism that had become standard in CGI fare.

16
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
Hotel Transylvania premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on September 8, 2012, and was
theatrically released in the United States on September 28, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

17
01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
It received mixed reviews from critics and  grossed $358
million against a budget of $85 million.

18
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
It was nominated for a Golden Globe for Best Animated Film.

19
01:18:35,454 --> 01:18:41,454
The financial success of Hotel Transylvania launched a
multimedia franchise, including three sequels.

20
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
The film explores themes of hotel, witch, vampire, romance, love.

21
01:26:51,818 --> 01:26:57,818
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
